{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional session-revocation feed poller (CONTRACT.md §10.4, contract 1.44 — AXIAM"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"threats T-39 and T-143)."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/effectivePollInterval","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/feedURL"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/isRevoked(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/refresh()"]},{"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/defaultPollInterval","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/feedPath","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/maxEntries","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/minPollInterval"]},{"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/entry(for:)"]},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/Actor-Implementations"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/revocationfeed"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Class","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RevocationFeed","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RevocationFeed"}],"title":"RevocationFeed","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK14RevocationFeedC","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"symbolKind":"class"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RevocationFeed","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"What this narrows, and what it is not","level":2,"anchor":"What-this-narrows-and-what-it-is-not"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An AXIAM access token is self-contained and valid for up to fifteen minutes, and this SDK"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verifies it locally. A logout, a role removal or an account disable therefore does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reach a token already in a caller’s hands until it expires — §10.2 records that, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"documented answer has been “route the decision through gRPC introspection instead”, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is correct and costs a round trip "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"per request"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A deployment may publish ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GET \/oauth2\/revocations"},{"text":": the base64url-unpadded SHA-256 of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every session id revoked within the last access-token lifetime. A guard that polls it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rejects a revoked session within ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one poll interval","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" instead of one token lifetime, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one cacheable fetch per interval.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is NOT a control, and every rule below follows from that:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Default off.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Nothing polls unless a caller constructs one and attaches it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Never on the request path.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/isRevoked(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" answers from the cached set and, at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most, refreshes a set the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"next","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" caller sees."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Never fail closed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" An unreachable feed, a non-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"200"},{"type":"text","text":", a body that does not parse, an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alg"},{"type":"text","text":" this build does not know — every one of them behaves exactly as no feed at all."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Not as an empty list: an empty list asserts that nothing has been revoked, which is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"guard that silently honours no revocations while appearing to honour them."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It only ever rejects.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Every §10.1 rule runs first and still decides. The feed can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"turn an accept into a reject and never the reverse.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A token with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sid"},{"type":"text","text":" is never matched."}]},{"type":"text","text":" There is no session behind a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"client-credentials token, an RPT or a token exchange, and hashing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jti"},{"type":"text","text":" instead would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match nothing while looking like it worked."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"actor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so one instance can be shared across guards and they poll once between them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than once each. Callers do not build one directly: set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamConfig\/revocationFeedEnabled","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" wires it to the same transport","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every other call already uses.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/ScA"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed"},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/ScA":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/ScA","title":"_Concurrency.Actor"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/RevocationFeed/refresh()":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fetches now, whatever the interval says. For tests, and for a caller that wants the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first poll to have happened before it starts serving."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/refresh()","role":"symbol","title":"refresh()","url":"\/d